  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and supporting documents and thereafter maintained as such for the lifetime of the development: - drawing number (add reference number)dated (date on the plans) - documents entitled (document title) dated (date on the document)",
    "Prior to commencement of the first occupation of the use a Detailed Management Plan shall be submitted to the Local Planning Authority. This document must include the following details:Executive OverviewStatement of purpose - clear description of the types of children the home will cater for (needs, disabilities, behavioural/ emotional requirements.Desired Outomes -&nbsp;stability, education, emotional development,\r\nindependence preparationState which regulatory bodies the home has been registered with and provide registration number.Management StructureOwnership / Responsible Individual – registered\r\n     provider and responsible individual details.Registered Manager – qualifications, responsibilities,\r\n     delegation of authority.Organisational Chart – clear hierarchy showing\r\n     accountability (manager, deputies, key workers, support staff, etc.).Risk Assessments –What risk assessments will be carried out regarding:Individual child risk assessmentsEnvironmental risk assessmentsFire safety, health &amp; safety, infection controlContact detailsA formal complaints process stating how complaints can be made, how they are acknowledged and logged and escalated where necessary (any email address must be generic, which goes to main inbox).Management of the rear garden,&nbsp;The development shall be operated in accordance with the approved Plan.Reason: To ensure safe and considerate operation of the site whilst also protecting the amenities of the nearby residents and surrounding area ensuring that any disruption is kept to a minimum in compliance with Policy 57 (Amenity) and Policy 58 (Making Places Safer and Designing Out Crime) of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024)."
